+# Planning-brief review
+
+Root read the complete final planning brief. Its final Born/Lüders clarification correctly separates instrument/condition compatibility from deriving probability values. The four-mode discriminator and covariance-family example are prospective acceptance controls, not campaign theorems or axiom countermodels. The actual axiom memo did not change in main66b; the brief retains its original7887 source pin. No new audit verdict or canonical science is asserted.
+
+Final brief SHA256: 1825debe48e14a60cc6ad0183661470aaa7d226485cf668c940c345e2c72712e
diff --git a/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-static-lower-20260907/NEXT_NATIVE_BRIDGE_CAMPAIGN.md b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-static-lower-20260907/NEXT_NATIVE_BRIDGE_CAMPAIGN.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..50d0dbe20b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-static-lower-20260907/NEXT_NATIVE_BRIDGE_CAMPAIGN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# Next campaign: make one native Record probability a physically identified observable
+
+Planning brief only,2026-09-07. No new theorem, experiment result, audit verdict or science PR is asserted here. The recommendation is deliberately narrower than “derive SU3”: test and, if possible, retire the preparation/condition bridge between an actual native Record instrument and the primitive local admissibility law before adding another encoded gauge Hamiltonian.
+
+## Grounding in the current foundation
+
+The authority inspected is `docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md` at main7887b4481feae2800c04c7c42ddac9554f2c2b9f, preserved locally as MINIMAL_AXIOMS_7887_REFERENCE.md (SHA93af34cf6fcfcfcc85c2cd39e8be7bbcf25253030f83a4cbc905a4a0cd68b753). This matters: the user's dirty checkout contains an older version and must not be used to reconstruct current premises.
+
+Current Admissibility supplies a fixed covariant nearest-neighbor probability distribution, conditional on formation, with available possibilities its support. It does not give the distribution's extensional form or values. Formation location/rate and an actual native measurement/process remain downstream. Current Record gives permanent locking, one Record/site and content-determined readout; it does NOT supply scalar finite additivity, an empty-record value, Born values or a log-det measure. The August distribution and additivity revisions must be carried into the next campaign's import ledger.
+
+The actual native flux work is a useful constraint, not a physical identification theorem:
+
+- Block21 uses a nine-mode/eight-physical-edge-qubit even-CAR code to read one low modular-flux bit by a bridge Record. Its encoding, preparation and port roles are supplied.
+- A single Gaussian-preprocessed bridge cannot read the carry-sensitive high bit on all inputs. Block25 strengthens this to a three-pair mean error at least1/3 for fixed positive orientation, and a four-test worst error at least1/4 for input-independent orientation mixtures. These bounds do not cover adaptive events.
+- The positive five-event escape uses twelve CAR modes/eleven physical edge qubits, four permanent low-history Records and a supplied sixteen-entry controller that chooses a native hopping pulse. It preserves basis data but records more than flux and is not a coherent flux-only Lüders instrument. Selective switching, pulse time, preparation and compatible energy apparatus remain imports.
+
+Thus programming the desired arithmetic into that controller would not identify its output with a physical gauge flux. Repeating its already known one-shot failure, or merely giving the controller a better battery, would not retire source/action selection.
+
+Blocks41–43 sharpen the other side: a supplied encoded full-irrep SU3 link is NOT an axiomatically native one-site qubit. Exact finite endpoint covariance is compatible with nonunitary transporter matrices, and the actual PW cutoff has norm-one top-shell defect. Energy-conditioned distinct-link approximations and charged bounds are available, but none constructs the encoding, prepares its physical ground, selects SU3 or fixes av. These results must not be imported as native gate availability.
+
+## One first target: conditional-state sufficiency for a native bridge Record
+
+**Concrete target.** Specify a framework-authorized map C_e from a candidate physical preparation to the actual nearest-neighbor conditions entering Admissibility, and a preparation domain D, then prove on the smallest nontrivial native block that the native formation instrument's complete output law factors through C_e:
+
+  p_e(z | rho, formation at e) = mu_e(z | C_e(rho)), for every rho in D.
+
+The map C_e must be identified from retained/native condition structure BEFORE choosing the target distribution. D cannot be selected after looking at the answer. The readout is the literal permanent physical edge-Z Record, not a numerical function of an unrecorded matter mode, a battery-energy readout, a controller table or a SU3 label.
+
+This is a prerequisite observable/source bridge: it asks whether the probability assigned by a supplied native CAR/Lüders instrument is really the primitive Record formation law on a declared physical condition domain. A positive result could retire that ONE instrument-to-Admissibility compatibility import. It would not yet retire the larger Wilson-action or physical-SU3-observable identification. That remaining distance must be explicit in the report.
+
+**Why this target before an action fit.** A reconstructed effective action is meaningless as a native derivation if changing an unregistered incoming preparation changes the “physical” Record odds at the same registered condition. Conversely, proving a condition-sufficient operational kernel supplies something that can later be tested for composition, locality and an action representation. No Wilson weight, beta value, maximum-entropy principle, detailed balance or additive readout is assumed to obtain it.
+
+## Minimal actual witness and an immediate falsifier
+
+Use a four-vertex CAR path with three physical edge qubits e0,e1,e2 in consecutive lattice sites. It has no cycle stabilizers; its even-parity code is the full eight-dimensional physical space. In the standard positive tree convention,
+
+ B0=Z0, B1=Z0Z1, B2=Z1Z2, B3=Z2,
+ n_j=(I-B_j)/2.
+
+Record the middle bridge e1 with the actual native projector Q_z=(I+zZ1)/2. Fix every exterior site, all old Records, apparatus readiness and event location identically. Keep all three edges initially live and use no incoming dwell. Test the two native product codewords
+
+ |100>_(e0,e1,e2)  <-> occupations(1,1,0,0),
+ |110>_(e0,e1,e2)  <-> occupations(1,0,1,0).
+
+Both have N=2 and the same two neighboring physical qubits: e0=1,e2=0. The middle native Record is deterministically + in the first and - in the second. This is a proposed hand-derived acceptance control to independently verify in the next campaign, not a newly audited claim here. It needs only literal8-by8 Pauli matrices and both complete sign branches; no SU3 encoding or generic quantum circuit is involved.
+
+This pair immediately refutes an UNRESTRICTED identification that (i) admits both preparations, (ii) defines C_e using only their identical neighbor data/old Records, and (iii) equates their native sharp measurement probabilities with a single neighbor-conditioned formation distribution. It does NOT refute Admissibility. Possible resolutions are that the preparations do not both belong to the actual admissible domain, that the registered physical conditions include additional legitimately derived data, or that this native measurement is not the primitive formation process. Those possibilities are precisely the bridge to settle.
+
+In particular do not assume that identical old Records imply identical complete nearest-neighbor conditions. The memo does not specify all such condition variables. The experiment must explicitly declare and justify C_e. Nor should one claim that measurement of an arbitrarily prepared incoming qubit is automatically the formation of a fresh primitive Record. Conflating these is the likely failure mode being tested.
+
+## Allowed imports, controls and completion criteria
+
+Allowed for the finite test: the actual tree BKSF dictionary and its legal-code theorem; the explicitly conditional native physical edge Record branches; finite matrix quantum mechanics for checking that instrument; a fixed supplied apparatus/readiness and a declared event at e1. These are marked imports, not consequences of M2(C) alone. Compatibility can retire only the declared instrument/condition identification. Born/Lüders probability values remain independent imports unless their own retained derivation is provided; consistency with a native condition map alone does not derive them. If a battery is introduced later, preserve its preparation, cap, refusal and readout contract; it is unnecessary for the first deterministic-sign control.
+
+Disallowed shortcuts: a freely supplied SU3 or Z4 encoder as “native,” a controller that evaluates the desired answer, selecting only successful signs, assigning probability values because a Born formula was programmed, deriving an action by defining minus-log of an already chosen Wilson distribution, or renaming the target's local incoming quantum state as a nearest-neighbor variable without a physical map.
+
+The first bounded session should produce:
+
+1. An exact source-side definition of C_e and D with every dependency classified. If none exists beyond conditional choices, record that fact before any parameter sweep.
+2. The literal native matrices for the two preparations and both branches, checking code legality, N, neighbor restrictions, old-Record preservation and complete probabilities. Then test any proposed domain restriction or condition map against this fixed pair and additional coherent states; do not retune it to exclude inconvenient data without a source reason.
+3. If a genuine condition-derived preparation channel E_C is proposed, derive it from the named admissibility structure and test whether all allowed realizations of E_C give the same complete Record law. Merely choosing E_C to manufacture mu_C is a failed derivation. Do not demand a coherence claim beyond the declared classical/quantum domain.
+
+**Success:** a retained-grounded condition/preparation theorem establishes the declared native instrument/condition identification on all allowed preparations. If Born/Lüders values are still supplied, state that the compatibility import alone has been retired; claiming the tested likelihoods themselves derived additionally requires their own retained derivation, without inserting those values. State exactly which probability/observable-identification import has disappeared and which action/group/coupling imports remain. A programmable implementation alone is not success.
+
+**Useful negative outcome:** give the explicit pair or compatible alternative preparations, the exact differing probabilities, and name the absent preparation/condition or formation-instrument identification. This excludes one proposed bridge/domain, not every possible native dynamics. Do not spend a full campaign republishing the already obvious unrestricted-preparation failure; use it as an early discriminator for serious proposed bridges.
+
+**Stop rule:** if the only offered “repair” is another chosen distribution, chosen controller or post hoc domain, there is no source/action retirement. Archive the precise failed proposal and switch lanes. Do not optimize batteries or enlarge the SU3 cutoff to disguise the missing premise.
+
+## A prospective condition-map discriminator supplied by root
+
+Root proposed a useful concrete candidate AFTER the initial brief was written. It fits the source-audit stage of the same condition-sufficiency target; it is not a second claimed result. If a pure-projector possibility domain, normalized spherical measure and an authorized comparison of neighboring internal frames have first been established, consider
+
+ dmu_kappa(n | neighbors)=[1+(kappa/6)sum_(recorded neighbors j) n dot m_j] dOmega(n)/(4pi),
+ with0<|kappa|<=1 and n dot m_j=2Tr(P(n)P(m_j))-1.
+
+The prospective discriminator is whether these ingredients are actually native-authorized, NOT whether one can write this positive normalized formula. Under the stated extra ingredients it appears to give a covariant family with one-neighbor moment kappa/18, so its parameter is a concrete possible residual even after normalization and cubic covariance. That formula and moment would need an independently reviewed calculation before appearing as campaign science.
+
+Crucially, M2(C) at each site does not by itself identify the two matrix algebras so that Tr(PP_j) is meaningful. Global SU2 covariance after choosing a common frame is weaker than independent local-frame covariance. An edge transport or other relative-frame structure may be required; a pure-projector-only physical domain and its readout also need authority. Without those bridges this is not an axiom-compatible countermodel and must not be reported as one.
+
+Use this as an early fork in the ONE proposed source audit: either identify a retained relative-frame/condition map and test whether kappa remains genuinely free, or record the exact missing intersite comparison premise before evaluating any physical odds. If kappa survives, the negative conclusion concerns the specified conditions plus covariance, not all possible admissibility laws. In neither case does a chosen kappa or a programmable readout select a Wilson coupling. The native Pauli bridge witness above then tests a concrete proposed formation-instrument identification on that registered condition domain; it cannot supply the missing frame by notation.
+
+## Comparison with the AC grain and readout obligations
+
+This test is worth prioritizing only if an actual retained candidate for C_e/D can be named. The current axioms by themselves do not supply the distribution's values, so I am uncertain that a positive bridge is presently ready. A short source audit may therefore be the decisive result, rather than a large computation.
+
+If no candidate exists, the exact AC obligations offer clearer physical closure targets than another supplied-Wilson extension:
+
+- `AC_ORBIT_OCCUPANCY_STATISTICAL_GRAIN_DERIVATION_OBLIGATION.md` requires the physical matter action AND measure that distinguish count-once det_C from count-twice |det_C|². A native CAR Fock encoding by itself does not identify that physical measure. This is the closest alternative because it directly targets a source/measure import.
+- `AC_RETA_HCLASS_HUNIT_READOUT_DERIVATION_OBLIGATION.md` requires a physical carrier/source bridge and a native eta/holonomy identity or genuinely inhomogeneous Record normalization theorem. Programming an angle readout or choosing a clock unit does not close it.
+- `THETA_QUARK_DETERMINANT_CROSS_SECTOR_READOUT_DERIVATION_OBLIGATION.md` additionally requires a quark determinant carrier and actual cross-sector identification. Shared algebra or a closed lepton grain gate would not suffice.
+
+These three July11 obligation files were read in the current-main priority worktree; they are open gates with no premise weight. The next campaign should select ONE proposed physical carrier and one exact closure criterion, not bundle their desired conclusions. If the native condition-sufficiency test cannot retire its narrow compatibility import, I would move next to the orbit-occupancy action/measure obligation, while retaining this test as a mandatory anti-circularity check for its proposed Record-facing carrier.
+
+## Evidence locations read for this brief
+
+Current axiom snapshot: main7887 `docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md`, especially Admissibility, Record, dynamics qualification, removed additivity and open gates. Native flux: `/private/tmp/toe-autonomous-orbital-20260907/native-flux-compiler/DERIVATION.md` and `adaptive/POSITIVE_ESCAPE_DERIVATION.md`. Robust bounds: `/private/tmp/toe-autonomous-native-ladder-20260907/robust-one-shot-review/REVIEW.md`. Finite bridge: own `finite-transporter-bridge/DERIVATION.md`, `finite-pw-charged-upper/DERIVATION.md`, `finite-pw-static-lower/DERIVATION.md`. No new live audit-status assertion or literature novelty claim is made by this planning memo.
