+
+Reviewed completed ROOT_DERIVATION.md SHA593c0cf58c849b6b3c368d748522a2df193fe387735aee75229f5d9f316b4260 only after native2037554d froze. PASS.
+
+The use of a separate finite-cutoff similarity centered on E0_R is essential and correctly implemented. The imported column estimate remains an explicit mathematical input with dimension-independent local gap/norm hypotheses; the source tensor contributes onlysqrt9. Full-irrep projection preserves component center covariance, the fundamental bare-path witness, and joint ghost vacuum. Finite-dimensional norm equivalence is used only for invertibility, not for uniform numerical bounds. The relative upper envelope algebra matches independent derivation and does not imply a charged-cost limit at fixedu.
+
+The optional EACH-fixed-R selected-GNS argument has the needed restrictions: fixed whole-range family, bounded local covariant tuples, finite-dimensional local normality, resolvent support transfer and nonzero local trial only undertheta<1. First-moment lower semicontinuity gives an upper bound, not equality. No finite charged minima convergence or R/volume interchange is asserted. Candidate and preliminary confirmations were exposed before root completion and are accurately disclosed. No correction requested.
