+# Root43 independent cold review
+
+PASS for ROOT_DERIVATION.md SHA593c0cf58c849b6b3c368d748522a2df193fe387735aee75229f5d9f316b4260. Read the complete proof after candidate exposure; native's completed43 proof has not yet been read. Uses the directly inspected Yarotsky0411042 Theorems1–3, Lemma1 and equations8–15 from the preceding independent reviews. No source edits.
+
+The proof correctly avoids subtracting uncut and cutoff variational floors. It reruns the coordinate estimate for H_R centered on E0_R. Complete PW cutoffs retain the unique constant vacuum and the fundamental irrep for everyR>=1, giving the same normalized onsite gap1. Compression decreases bounded face norms and leaves the fixed range unchanged. The source theorem permits arbitrary onsite Hilbert spaces and imposes no upper onsite-energy bound; its constants depend on the fixed range and a chosen decay parameter, not dimension. Fixing those choices once therefore gives common smallness/column constants for allR. This is an expressly imported uniformity claim, not an estimate inferred from finite tests.
+
+Gauge factorization over outgoing cells survives full-irrep compression. Vacuum-overlap normalization and uniqueness of the creation logarithm make the similarity gauge-equivariant. The component-center argument requires all actual boundary Gauss conditions, as retained. Occupied links in any charged component must connect both sources, and each costs at least1 in scaled energy; higher irreps and baryonic vertices cannot lower the floor. The distinction between occupied links and occupied cells is explicit. The fundamental simple-path vacuum vector is retained forR1 and proves nonemptiness without using its extensive potential energy as an upper bound.
+
+The source9 extension costs3 by component Cauchy–Schwarz. The coordinate excitation projectors preserve the charged restriction; each nonzero charged block has H_I>=d. Thus H0(H0-z)^-1 has the claimed l1 block bound, and the Neumann inverse excludes every realz<(1-kappa)d. Finite dimension removes domain/closure ambiguity, but the argument still uses the exact coordinate restriction rather than unlabelled spectral circles. The vacuum subtracted is precisely E0_R.
+
+Ghost links are decoupled and their joint vacuum is preserved by the ground/log/similarity construction, as established in38. Restricting before applying the free floor prevents any ghost shortcut; zero ghost ground energy leaves the actual vacuum subtraction unchanged. Merely bounding the padded graph distance instead would not suffice, but the proof does not do that.
+
+Dividing the reviewed42 upper numerator by4d/a gives exactly B=[1+sqrt(theta)(1+sqrt(8u)+2u)+2u sqrt(32u/h_R)]/(1-theta). At fixedu and h_R/d tending to infinity, theta tends to0 and h_R tends to infinity, so B tends to1. This is only a bound on possible ratios; no ratio convergence or equality is inferred. The explicit failure of the sufficient upper normalization condition at fixedR and arbitrary growingd remains intact.
+
+For the optional fixedR GNS extension, the full local matrix algebra has automatic normality, and the same finite gauge-average density argument applies. The bounded local compressed path tuple has norm squared q_Lambda>=1-theta; local-state convergence gives q_infinity>0. Applying local weak resolvent convergence to its unnormalized components and dividing by q_Lambda tending to q_infinity gives the claimed normalized spectral-measure convergence. Nonnegative first-moment lower semicontinuity gives the upper form bound, while support exclusion gives the lower bound. No convergence of charged minimizers, jointR/volume limit or bottom eigenvector follows. No correction requested.
