@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Root43 prospective finite-cutoff charged lower bound
+
+Final campaign stretch after42. Candidate exposed to native before completed proofs: redo38's ground-similarity and charged coordinate-resolvent argument for the ACTUAL full-irrep cutoff, using34's uniform local-gap/perturbation hypotheses. The inequality cannot be obtained by subtracting independent uncut variational inequalities, because the neutral vacuum energy also changes under cutoff. Require the lower constant to be independent of R>=1, volume and separation; check exact Gauss covariance, component-center free floor, nine-component source amplification, ghost-vacuum restriction and nonempty finite charged sector. Then combine the independently proved42 upper bound without claiming convergence of charged minima or a fixed-cutoff all-distance upper bound. A fixed-R selected infinite-representation extension is optional only if weak-resolvent and nonzero local-trial arguments are explicit.
+
+Finite controls should include actual R=1 graph color/triality support with boundary Gauss imposed, the invalid vacuum-subtraction inference as an adverse, and exact dimensionless upper-envelope behavior. These cannot numerically verify the imported theorem or locate its smallness threshold. No new hardware compiler or axiom-selected action is in scope.
diff --git a/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-static-lower-20260907/evidence/root/ROOT_DERIVATION.md b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-static-lower-20260907/evidence/root/ROOT_DERIVATION.md
